The attached image illustrates that Nano-11 enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel A, displaying flow cytometry dot plots, shows minimal uptake of soluble ovalbumin (OVA) alone, while Nano-11 is readily taken up. When OVA is adsorbed to Nano-11 (Nano-11+OVA), there is a significant increase in OVA-containing BMDCs compared to soluble OVA alone. Panel B's histogram further confirms this, showing a substantial shift to higher fluorescence intensity for Nano-11+OVA, indicating improved antigen delivery to antigen-presenting cells and contributing to Nano-11's immunostimulatory properties.